 34SI c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL/MSU), August 4, 2017                         
 34SI c  2017Ha23: {+34}Al source was produced by fragmentation of E=69.2       
 34SI2c  MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar beam from the Heavy Ion Research Facility in       
 34SI3c  Lanzhou (HIRFL) on 182.6 mg/cm{+2} thick {+9}Be target. Fragments were 
 34SI4c  identified based on energy loss, time-of-flight, and magnetic rigidity 
 34SI5c  on an event-by-event basis, and implanted into a 1500-|mm-thick        
 34SI6c  double-sided Si strip detector (DSSD) between two plastic              
 34SI7c  scintillators. |b-delayed |g rays were detected by two Ge clover       
 34SI8c  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, E|b, I|b, |g|g-coin, |g|b(t). Deduced    
 34SI9c  levels, parent half-life. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.   
